The problem statement mentions that it must parse the comments starting with '@@@' and generate code snippet based on them. The '@@@' comments in the provided C# code provide information about the expected behaviour of the test - "index of x after setting is more than or same as zero". This translates to the assertion that New_arrListIndexOfX (the updated index of x) must be greater or equal to zero, so the Debug.Assert statement to generate looks something like: Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >=0). The generated code snippet will be inserted into the relevant tests in the test method (PUT_SetContract in this case).--------------------
